From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: gen1: honour a GOP size of 0

V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_GOP_SIZE accepts 0, which clients such as the
Android Codec2 V4L2 HAL use to say that they request key frames
themselves and want no periodic intra frames. iris_set_intra_period()
returns -EINVAL for it, and the caller ignores the error, so no
HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_INTRA_PERIOD reaches the gen1 firmware. Without
that property the firmware codes every frame as an intra frame: a
300-frame 1080p encode came out with 300 key frames.

Send the longest intra period instead, 0x0fffffff P-frames, the value
Qualcomm's own drivers send for an unlimited GOP. B-frames keep their
existing handling, and other GOP sizes are converted as before.

Checked on SC8280XP (Huawei MateBook E Go) with a Codec2 HAL that sets
GOP_SIZE to 0: 300-frame HEVC and H.264 encodes with a 5 s key frame
interval at 30 fps have key frames at frames 0 and 150 only, and with
no key frame interval only at frame 0.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c | 29 +++++++++++++------
 .../qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h         |  3 ++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
index c9a143b913..bcb4cd7f2a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
@@ -1389,16 +1389,27 @@ int iris_set_intra_period(struct iris_inst *inst, enum platform_inst_fw_cap_type
 	u32 hfi_id = inst->fw_caps[cap_id].hfi_id;
 	struct hfi_intra_period intra_period;
 
-	if (!gop_size || b_frame >= gop_size)
-		return -EINVAL;
+	if (!gop_size) {
+		/*
+		 * A GOP size of 0 asks for no periodic intra frames: the client
+		 * requests key frames itself (V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FORCE_KEY_FRAME).
+		 * The firmware has no such mode, and without an intra period it
+		 * codes every frame as an intra frame, so give it the longest one.
+		 */
+		intra_period.pframes = HFI_INTRA_PERIOD_MAX_PFRAMES;
+		intra_period.bframes = b_frame;
+	} else {
+		if (b_frame >= gop_size)
+			return -EINVAL;
 
-	/*
-	 * intra_period represents the length of a GOP, which includes both P-frames
-	 * and B-frames. The counts of P-frames and B-frames within a GOP must be
-	 * communicated to the firmware.
-	 */
-	intra_period.pframes = (gop_size - 1) / (b_frame + 1);
-	intra_period.bframes = b_frame;
+		/*
+		 * intra_period represents the length of a GOP, which includes both
+		 * P-frames and B-frames. The counts of P-frames and B-frames within
+		 * a GOP must be communicated to the firmware.
+		 */
+		intra_period.pframes = (gop_size - 1) / (b_frame + 1);
+		intra_period.bframes = b_frame;
+	}
 
 	return hfi_ops->session_set_property(inst, hfi_id,
 					     HFI_HOST_FLAGS_NONE,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h
index 1a2e83f7b1..05ff022ad5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h
@@ -497,6 +497,9 @@ struct hfi_max_num_b_frames {
 	u32 max_num_b_frames;
 };
 
+/* P-frame count Qualcomm's drivers send in hfi_intra_period for an unlimited GOP */
+#define HFI_INTRA_PERIOD_MAX_PFRAMES	0x0fffffff
+
 struct hfi_intra_period {
 	u32 pframes;
 	u32 bframes;
